# Android differences from upstream

Android enables arithmetic encoding and decoding to preserve support for JPEG
files that use arithmetic coding. Both macros are defined in `src/jconfig.h`
and `src/jconfigint.h` so library users receive the matching error codes.

The generated configuration headers support Android target architectures and
host builds from one source tree. RISC-V uses the scalar implementation because
Android does not currently compile this module with the RVV ISA extension.

`src/jpeglib.h` retains Chromium's optional `MANGLE_JPEG_NAMES` integration.
The Android modules use the standard libjpeg symbol names.
